00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:10.132
And this is going to be related
to the main energy, kind

00:14:10.132 --> 00:14:12.301
of e, 1, 1, right?

00:14:12.301 --> 00:14:13.135
E, 2, 2.

00:14:13.135 --> 00:14:16.839
So this is going to be related
to the main energy level.

00:14:16.839 --> 00:14:22.611
Main energy level, right?

00:14:22.611 --> 00:14:26.715
And it's also related
to the radial distance.

00:14:26.715 --> 00:14:28.317
Radial distance.

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.857
And sometimes we
call this the shell.

00:14:34.857 --> 00:14:36.826
So sometimes the
principal quantum number,

00:14:36.826 --> 00:14:38.794
this is the shell, right?

00:14:38.794 --> 00:14:42.031
It's the first shell,
or the second shell.

00:14:42.031 --> 00:14:45.201
So we can call this the shell.

00:14:45.201 --> 00:14:47.536
Come back to that later.

00:14:47.536 --> 00:14:49.305
And you can see right there.

00:14:49.305 --> 00:14:51.907
OK, we'll talk about n
equals 2 and 3 in a second.

00:14:51.907 --> 00:14:55.344
But you know-- oh,
let's talk about it now.

00:14:55.344 --> 00:14:56.779
You can see right there--

00:14:56.779 --> 00:15:03.352
it I go from n equals 1 to n
equals 2, then I'm further out.

00:15:03.352 --> 00:15:05.020
Yeah, I still got non-0.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:07.923
Doesn't quite go to 0
like I just said there.

00:15:07.923 --> 00:15:10.593
But it's further out,
it's shifted out, right?

00:15:10.593 --> 00:15:13.796
So with increasing n--

00:15:13.796 --> 00:15:15.764
so another thing
we can say about n

00:15:15.764 --> 00:15:34.750
is that with increasing n, you
get higher energies and larger

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:35.651
distances.

00:15:35.651 --> 00:15:38.520
larger r, a [? hole. ?]

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.689
But you get something else.

00:15:40.689 --> 00:15:43.158
You get something else,
and you can see it there.

00:15:43.158 --> 00:15:45.794
And I've been avoiding it, but
I got to address it right now.

00:15:45.794 --> 00:15:49.732
Because those higher
end functions go to 0.

00:15:49.732 --> 00:15:51.700
So they have nodes.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:55.571
With increasing n,
you get more nodes.

00:15:55.571 --> 00:15:56.205
What's a node?

00:15:56.205 --> 00:15:58.941
A node is when it goes to 0.

00:15:58.941 --> 00:16:00.542
And there's more of them.

00:16:00.542 --> 00:16:02.811
Now that's also
really important.

00:16:05.948 --> 00:16:13.822
So what that means is in
Bohr, my orbit was r, e.

00:16:13.822 --> 00:16:16.659
Heisenberg said no way.

00:16:16.659 --> 00:16:17.660
Can't have them both.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:21.063
But I had a r,
which was one value.

00:16:21.063 --> 00:16:22.831
And remember-- it
could only then

00:16:22.831 --> 00:16:26.969
be the r of the next
value, the next n.

00:16:26.969 --> 00:16:29.171
Now I'm basically
saying the opposite.

00:16:29.171 --> 00:16:32.040
I'm saying, well actually,
