probability, except not here.

00:16:41.517 --> 00:16:43.285
In this one place.

00:16:43.285 --> 00:16:44.486
This node.

00:16:44.486 --> 00:16:45.354
It's 0.

00:16:45.354 --> 00:16:46.755
It's literally 0.

00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:49.491
The probability of finding
the electron there is 0.

00:16:49.491 --> 00:16:50.726
It cannot exist there.

00:16:50.726 --> 00:16:52.962
But how bizarre is that?

00:16:52.962 --> 00:16:57.967
The electron can exist
with probability out here,

00:16:57.967 --> 00:17:02.137
and probability in here, but
it can't exist in between.

00:17:02.137 --> 00:17:05.340
It's the same electron.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:08.042
Try explaining how it
goes back and forth.

00:17:08.042 --> 00:17:13.515
It skips over a zero
probability part, r.

00:17:13.515 --> 00:17:14.016
Right?

00:17:14.016 --> 00:17:15.684
But these nodes
are very important.

00:17:15.684 --> 00:17:18.186
And just to give you a
