00:19:11.733 --> 00:19:14.002
only to its square.

00:19:14.002 --> 00:19:16.138
So we go about our business
for the last 100 years

00:19:16.138 --> 00:19:18.340
squaring it and saying, OK,
well it describes nature.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:18.907
That's great.

00:19:18.907 --> 00:19:23.712
But no one, still, knows what
it means without the square.

00:19:23.712 --> 00:19:24.913
I find that incredible.

00:19:24.913 --> 00:19:28.584
And it led Bohr to say all
sorts of really cool things.

00:19:28.584 --> 00:19:31.653
He said, "We must be clear
that when it comes to atoms,

00:19:31.653 --> 00:19:36.225
language can be used
only as in poetry.

00:19:36.225 --> 00:19:38.760
The poet, too, is not
nearly so concerned

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:41.797
